More on unnecessary verbage:
I think there needs to be an "ignore-space" option.  I really
hate the "Unknown command ' '." message ... but I don't want to set 
"rest-on-space".   Plain hack used to just beep when you hit space.
At 1200 baud one gets tired of waiting for all the "unknown command..."
messages to clear off.  Lets either bring back the old behavior or 
add an "ignore-space" option!

Also, if you use "-u" (i.e. 'nethack -uChuck-w') then the program
should not print the copyright notice (from u_init()...).  Or if
the dev team insists on the notice, you should at least reduce it down
to one (short) line instead of three... 

Chuck [using 3.0i pl 9]

